  "id": "modernization",
  "term": "modernization",
  "definition": "Modernization refers to broad social changes such as urbanization, market integration, formal schooling, language shift, and cultural commodification that reshape how well-being is understood and maintained. In this context, it can place Indigenous identities, knowledge, and practices under outside standards of value, with possible effects on belonging, cultural continuity, and sense of self.",
